            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "NFPA guidance calls for a CO alarm outside each separate sleeping area, in the immediate vicinity of the bedrooms, and on every level of the home including the basement. Add one near fuel-burning appliances and the door to an attached garage. Follow the manual's instructions on height and distance from appliances, and keep alarms out of bathrooms and direct sunlight."
